From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] regmap: slimbus: pass the device itself as the bus context

The bus callbacks take their context as a struct slim_device, but
__devm_regmap_init_slimbus() passed &slimbus, the address of its own
parameter on the stack, so every transfer of a devm slimbus regmap went
through a dangling pointer. It oopsed in slim_do_transfer() on the first
write. __regmap_init_slimbus() passed &slimbus->dev, which only works
because dev is the first member of struct slim_device.

Pass slimbus in both, as upstream has since done.

---
--- a/drivers/base/regmap/regmap-slimbus.c
+++ b/drivers/base/regmap/regmap-slimbus.c
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(bus))
 		return ERR_CAST(bus);
 
-	return __regmap_init(&slimbus->dev, bus, &slimbus->dev, config,
+	return __regmap_init(&slimbus->dev, bus, slimbus, config,
 			     lock_key, lock_name);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(__regmap_init_slimbus);
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(bus))
 		return ERR_CAST(bus);
 
-	return __devm_regmap_init(&slimbus->dev, bus, &slimbus, config,
+	return __devm_regmap_init(&slimbus->dev, bus, slimbus, config,
 				  lock_key, lock_name);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(__devm_regmap_init_slimbus);
